      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-47486",
      ":question/problem": "The altitude of an apple that is dropped from the top of a building, measured in meters, is given by the function $s(t)$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. The values of $s(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $s(t)$ | $417$ | $412$ | $397$ | $373$ | $339$ |\n\nApproximate the velocity $s^{\u2032}(t)$ when $t = 2$ using a backward difference approximation.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
