      ":question/problem": "A factory produces pencils. The total cost of producing $x$ pencils, measured in cents, is given by the function $C(x)$. The values of $C(x)$ for different values of $x$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $10$ | $20$ | $30$ | $40$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $C(x)$ | $0$ | $7$ | $13$ | $18$ | $23$ |\n\nApproximate the marginal cost $C^{\u2032}(x)$ at the point $x = 40$ using a backward difference approximation.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
